High-ranking UN officials cancelled visits to Pakistan due to flights
ISLAMBURG (AFP) The incoming president of the United Nations General Assembly announced on Sunday that he had postponed his visit to Pakistan due to technical problems.
Last month, Turkish diplomat Volkan Bozkir was successfully elected president of the 75th session of the United Nations General Assembly, which was scheduled to arrive in Islamabad on Sunday.
However, he tweeted that plans to visit Pakistan's capital had to be postponed.
Pakistan's Foreign Minister Shah Mahmood Qureshi tweeted in response to Bozkir, saying that he warmly welcomes you to visit Pakistan as soon as possible for a constructive and fruitful visit.
Just a day earlier, Qureshi Singh announced the visit with great enthusiasm, expressing his desire to discuss a series of issues with Bozkir, including Kashmir, which lies between Pakistan and neighbouring India, both of which claim sovereignty over the entire Kashmir region.
Since independence from British rule in 1947, there have been three wars between Pakistan and India, both involving the disputed region.
The two sides frequently clashed in Kashmir, causing military and civilian casualties.
Pakistan wants the United Nations to pass a resolution allowing people living in the Himalayas to decide whether to merge with India or Pakistan and thus advance the Kashmir issue.
Manchester United get a European Cup ticket and Paul Pogba suggests staying with the team
After the Red Devils were locked in the top four, Manchester United star Paul Pogba hinted that he would remain with the team this summer.
A 2-0 win over Leicester City meant Manchester United ended up in third place ahead of Frank Lampard's Chelsea team.
Leicester City were still 14 points ahead of Manchester United in 12 games, but the Red Devils were on their way to a fourth-place finish.
